id: pm-web-fhob
title: Make spawn-overlap regression independent of process startup scheduling
description: "The unchanged spawn-fallback regression in test/pm-runner.test.ts failed during PR #176 standalone validation with SDK 2026.10.10. It observed start first, end first, start independent, end independent, start second, end second. Same-workspace serialization held, but the independent child did not start within the first child 120 ms delay under heavy shared verification load. Use an explicit ready/release protocol to prove independent dispatch without depending on process startup order; preserve real subprocess assertions and timeout behavior. This is a test-reliability follow-up, not an established SDK dispatch defect. Do not relax coverage, duplication or graph timing gates."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T05:41:15.955Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:47.898Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:47.424Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:37:47.424Z"
author: codex-attestation
resolution: "Reverified main ca7e188bc91e (unchanged since audit): [PR #197](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/197) repairs the process-order fixture with an explicit ready/release protocol. Other later shared-load startup failures are separately tracked by qdhx. Retained evidence: src/services/package-catalog.ts, test/catalog-install-e2e.test.ts, test/catalog.test.ts."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T05:46:04.382Z",codex-attestation,The completed first standalone npm run preserves the startup-order failure receipt; the attempted local Bun gate was intentionally interrupted by the orchestrator to avoid further shared-host contention. No runner production code or assertion is changed in PR #176. Independent CI on the pushed head remains the next evidence source; keep this follow-up open.
